{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>I have heard the murmurings of the children of Israel.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: even though the children of Israel murmur, they are still My children, they are My beloved, they are the seed of Abraham My beloved. <b>Speak to them, saying.</b> What is the meaning of לאמר (saying)? It teaches that he should speak to them partly harshly and partly gently, for the language of דבור (speak) is a language of harshness, as it is said (Genesis 42:30): ״דבר האישׁ אדוני הארץ אתנו קשות״ — the man, the lord of the land, spoke harshly to us." "<b>And in the morning you shall be satisfied with bread, and you shall know that I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> That you shall bless My name over the food, in the manner of what is written (Deuteronomy 8:10): ״ואכלת ושבעת וברכת את ה׳ אלהיך״ — and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless YHWH your Elohim. And from here our Rabbis of blessed memory said: Moses instituted for Israel the blessing of the Provider (הזן) at the time the manna descended for them. And from this they said: the blessing after the meal (ברכת המזון) is from the Torah, but the blessing of המוציא is rabbinic, from a fortiori reasoning: if when he is satisfied he blesses, when he is hungry how much more so."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:00:03.032092186Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}